Embedded React: a border sweep, a light travelling around a View's rounded edge.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/include/er_scene.h,
engine/scene/er_node_internal.h, engine/scene/compositor.c,
engine/animation/animation.c, engine/CMakeLists.txt,
bridges/quickjs/native_ui_bridge.c,
bridges/quickjs/js/src/embedded-react/index.d.ts,
engine/tests/rendering/CMakeLists.txt and the new
engine/rendering/border_sweep.c, engine/rendering/border_sweep.h and
engine/tests/rendering/test_border_sweep.c. Proposed upstream, with the other
border ring patches, as pull request #325.

The PS5 focus ring is a continuous light running around the focused item's
rounded border, bright at its head and fading in a long tail. Points moved by
Animated could only approximate it. View styles borderSweepColor,
borderSweepWidth, borderSweepLength and borderSweepPhase draw a ring of that
width inside the box, over the content, following the corner radius,
anti-aliased on both edges, with alpha falling off behind the head along the
perimeter. borderSweepPhase is animatable by the native driver (wrapping at 1),
and a phase-only change damages the bands along the four edges the ring can
reach rather than the whole box. A transformed (scaled) node still repaints
its whole transformed box.

